       "desc": "EmbeddingGemma 2 (`google/embeddinggemma-2`) single-vector embedding encoder (arch 18): 24 bidirectional Gemma-4-family layers (sliding/full 5:1, per-layer head_dim/KV overrides, half-split RoPE, projection-only PLE, sandwich norms, `layer_scalar`), mean pool + L2 into the 768-d `embedding_projection`, Matryoshka 768/512/256/128 via the request's `dims`. **Not a chat model** — no LM head, served only through the non-chat `embed` verb (`hipfire embed`, `POST /v1/embeddings`). Text, image, audio and video: the checkpoint's vision and audio towers ride the `<trunk-stem>.vl` pack declared in `vision`, and the video leg drives that same vision tower per frame (no extra weights). Tower VRAM follows `vision_mode`, which defaults to `auto` (the pack is loaded and media served; `vision_mode=off` keeps the load text-only, media refused per modality). LOCAL-ONLY staged artifact, NOT uploaded/pullable: produced with `hipfire-quantize --input <google/embeddinggemma-2 snapshot> --output <this file> --format mq4v2`, which writes the tower pack beside it; place both in the models directory. The digests are of the bytes that command reproduced, so a re-quantized artifact carries different ones. Parity against a float32 CPU transformers 5.19.0 reference (2e-2 rel-L2 band, `scripts/check_embeddinggemma2_parity.py`): text 2.2e-4-1.0e-3, images 2.7e-4-3.1e-3, audio 2.4e-4-2.6e-3, video 3.1e-4-4.9e-3 on the raw checkpoint; on this mq4v2 trunk the worst fixture is 2.75e-1 against its 5e-1 band, and `scripts/check_embeddinggemma2_multislot.py` is bit-identical to the sequential route with mixed media in one batched forward.",
